L2467@P81: A5-82 Copyright © 2003-2020 Arm Limited or its affiliates. All rights reserved. ARM IHI 0022H
L2468@P81: Non-Confidential ID040120
L2469@P81: For write response, the interconnect uses the additional bits of the BID identifier to determine which master port the
L2470@P81: write response is destined for. The interconnect removes these bits of the BID identifier before passing the BID
L2471@P81-82: value to the correct master port.ARM IHI 0022H Copyright © 2003-2020 Arm Limited or its affiliates. All rights reserved. A6-83
L2472@P82: ID040120 Non-Confidential
L2473@P82: Chapter A6
L2474@P82: AXI Ordering Model
L2475@P82: This chapter specifies:
L2476@P82: • AXI ordering model overview on page A6-84
L2477@P82: • Memory locations and Peripheral regions on page A6-85
L2478@P82: • Transactions and ordering on page A6-86
L2479@P82: • Observation and completion definitions on page A6-87
L2480@P82: • Master ordering guarantees on page A6-88
L2481@P82: • Ordering requirements on page A6-89
L2482@P82: • Response before the endpoint on page A6-90
L2483@P82-83: • Ordered write observation on page A6-91A6 AXI Ordering Model
L2484@P83: A6.1 AXI ordering model overview
L2485@P83: A6-84 Copyright © 2003-2020 Arm Limited or its affiliates. All rights reserved. ARM IHI 0022H
L2486@P83: Non-Confidential ID040120
L2487@P83: A6.1 AXI ordering model overview
L2488@P83: The AXI ordering model is based on the use of the transaction identifier, which is signaled on ARID or AWID.
L2489@P83: Transaction requests on the same channel, with the same ID and destination are guaranteed to remain in order.
L2490@P83: Transaction responses with the same ID are returned in the same order as the requests were issued.
L2491@P83: The ordering model does not give any ordering guarantees between:
L2492@P83: • Transactions from different masters
L2493@P83: • Read and write transactions
L2494@P83: • Transactions with different IDs
L2495@P83: • Transactions to different Peripheral regions
L2496@P83: • Transactions to different Memory locations
L2497@P83: If a master requires ordering between transactions that have no ordering guarantee, the master must wait to receive
L2498@P83-84: a response to the first transaction before issuing the second transaction.A6 AXI Ordering Model
L2499@P84: A6.2 Memory locations and Peripheral regions
L2500@P84: ARM IHI 0022H Copyright © 2003-2020 Arm Limited or its affiliates. All rights reserved. A6-85
L2501@P84: ID040120 Non-Confidential
L2502@P84: A6.2 Memory locations and Peripheral regions
L2503@P84: The address map in AMBA is made up of Memory locations and Peripheral regions.
L2504@P84: A Memory location has all of the following properties:
L2505@P84: • A read of a byte from a Memory location returns the last value that was written to that byte location.
L2506@P84: • A write to a byte of a Memory location updates the value at that location to a new value that is obtained by
L2507@P84: a subsequent read of that location.
L2508@P84: • Reading or writing to a Memory location has no side-effects on any other Memory location.
L2509@P84: • Observation guarantees for Memory are given for each location.
L2510@P84: • The size of a Memory location is equal to the single-copy atomicity size for that component.
L2511@P84: A Peripheral region has all of the following properties:
L2512@P84: • A read from an address in a Peripheral region does not necessarily return the last value that is written to that
L2513@P84: address.
L2514@P84: • A write to a byte address in a Peripheral region does not necessarily update the value at that address to a new
L2515@P84: value that is obtained by subsequent reads.
L2516@P84: • Accessing an address within a Peripheral region might have side-effects on other addresses within that
L2517@P84: region.
L2518@P84: • Observation guarantees for Peripherals are given per region.
L2519@P84: • The size of a Peripheral region is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED, but it must be contained within a single slave
L2520@P84-85: component.A6 AXI Ordering Model
L2521@P85: A6.3 Transactions and ordering
L2522@P85: A6-86 Copyright © 2003-2020 Arm Limited or its affiliates. All rights reserved. ARM IHI 0022H
L2523@P85: Non-Confidential ID040120
L2524@P85: A6.3 Transactions and ordering
L2525@P85: A transaction is a read or a write to one or more address locations. The locations are determined by AxADDR and
L2526@P85: any relevant qualifiers such as the Non-secure bit in AxPROT.
L2527@P85: • Ordering guarantees are given only between accesses to the same Memory location or Peripheral region.
L2528@P85: • A transaction to a Peripheral region must be entirely contained within that region.
L2529@P85: • A transaction that spans multiple Memory locations has multiple ordering guarantees.
L2530@P85: Transactions can be either of type Device or Normal:
L2531@P85: Device A read or write where the request has AxCACHE[1] deasserted.
L2532@P85: Device transactions can be used to access Peripheral regions or Memory locations.
L2533@P85: Normal A read or write where the request has AxCACHE[1] asserted.
L2534@P85: Normal transactions are used to access Memory locations and are not expected to be used to access
L2535@P85: Peripheral regions.
L2536@P85: A Normal access to a Peripheral region must complete in a protocol-compliant manner, but the
L2537@P85: result is IMPLEMENTATION DEFINED.
L2538@P85: A write transaction can be either Non-bufferable or Bufferable. It is possible to send an early response to Bufferable
L2539@P85: writes.
L2540@P85: • A Non-bufferable write has AWCACHE[0] deasserted.
L2541@P85-86: • A Bufferable write has AWCACHE[0] asserted.A6 AXI Ordering Model
L2542@P86: A6.4 Observation and completion definitions
L2543@P86: ARM IHI 0022H Copyright © 2003-2020 Arm Limited or its affiliates. All rights reserved. A6-87
L2544@P86: ID040120 Non-Confidential
L2545@P86: A6.4 Observation and completion definitions
L2546@P86: For accesses to Peripheral regions, a Device read or write access DRW1 is observed by a Device read or write access
L2547@P86: DRW2, when DRW1 arrives at the slave component before DRW2.
L2548@P86: For accesses to Memory locations, all of the following apply:
L2549@P86: • A write W1 is observed by a write W2, if W2 takes effect after W1.
L2550@P86: • A read R1 is observed by a write W2, if R1 returns data from a write W3, when W2 is after W3.
L2551@P86: • A write W1 is observed by a read R2, if R2 returns data from either W1 or from write W3, when W3 is after
L2552@P86: W1.
L2553@P86: Read R1 or write W1 can be of type Device or Normal.
L2554@P86: The definitions of write and read completions are:
L2555@P86: Write completion response
L2556@P86: The cycle when the associated BRESP handshake is given, when BVALID and BREADY are
L2557@P86: asserted.
L2558@P86: Read completion response
L2559@P86: The cycle when the last associated RDATA handshake is given, when RVALID, RLAST and
L2560@P86-87: RREADY are asserted.A6 AXI Ordering Model
L2561@P87: A6.5 Master ordering guarantees
