L2563@P87: Non-Confidential ID040120
L2564@P87: A6.5 Master ordering guarantees
L2565@P87: There are three types of ordering model guarantees:
L2566@P87: • Observability guarantees before a completion response is received.
L2567@P87: • Observability guarantees from a completion response.
L2568@P87: • Response ordering guarantees.
L2569@P87: A6.5.1 Guarantees before a completion response is received
L2570@P87: All of the following guarantees apply to transactions from the same master, using the same ID:
L2571@P87: • A Device write DW1 is guaranteed to arrive at the destination before Device write DW2, where DW2 is
L2572@P87: issued after DW1 and to the same Peripheral region.
L2573@P87: • A Device read DR1 is guaranteed to arrive at the destination before Device read DR2, where DR2 is issued
L2574@P87: after DR1 and to the same Peripheral region.
L2575@P87: • A write W1 is guaranteed to be observed by a write W2, where W2 is issued after W1 and to the same
L2576@P87: Memory location.
L2577@P87: • A write W1 that has been observed by a read R2 is guaranteed to be observed by a read R3, where R3 is issued
L2578@P87: after R2 and to the same Memory location.
L2579@P87: The guarantees imply that there are ordering guarantees between Device and Normal accesses to the same Memory
L2580@P87: location.
L2581@P87: A6.5.2 Guarantees from a completion response
L2582@P87: A completion response guarantees all of the following:
L2583@P87: • A completion response to a read request guarantees that it is observable to a subsequent read or write request
L2584@P87: from any master.
L2585@P87: • A completion response to a write request guarantees that it is observable to a subsequent read or write request

